WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.880
SAT tutors and programs follow a fixed plan built to fill the hour.

00:04.340 --> 00:07.400
Same general curriculum for every student, one topic a week.

00:08.000 --> 00:10.940
And while that works for some people, that's not how I teach.

00:11.700 --> 00:14.320
Before our first session, you take a full-length diagnostic.

00:14.740 --> 00:19.140
It's free, and I come back with an analysis of every answer and every behavior.

00:19.720 --> 00:22.960
How long you spent on each question, whether you switched answers,

00:23.220 --> 00:25.880
and whether you used the right approach for that question type.

00:26.360 --> 00:29.120
By the time we meet, I know exactly where the points are.

00:29.120 --> 00:31.520
In our sessions, I work from that data.

00:32.080 --> 00:34.760
When you miss a question, I already know what kind of mistake it was.

00:35.100 --> 00:38.520
And the next question I give you is picked to fix that exact thing.

00:39.620 --> 00:42.720
As one of my private students, you'll have direct access to my platform.

00:43.260 --> 00:48.020
SAT courses, curated practice tests, over 4,000 practice questions and more.

00:48.740 --> 00:54.120
Any questions or extra help go through a direct message or my weekly office hours.

00:54.560 --> 00:56.620
And parents get an update after every session:

00:57.240 --> 01:00.960
what we worked on, how the practice went, study habits, and any new scores.

01:01.760 --> 01:04.380
Some of my students have six months, some have two weeks.

01:04.880 --> 01:08.560
Either way, we build the plan around your test date and your target score,

01:08.740 --> 01:11.240
and you see it in writing before we start.

01:12.140 --> 01:14.780
Personal, responsive, and built around one student at a time.
